BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:the-bear-chase-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260927T000000Z
DTSTART:20261003T053000Z
DTEND:20261003T093000Z
SUMMARY:The Bear Chase
DESCRIPTION:The Bear Chase Race Endurance Festival is a multi-distance trail running event featuring 100K\, 50 Mile\, 50K\, Half Marathon\, 10K\, and 5K distances at Bear Creek Lake Park in Lakewood\, CO. The course is relatively fast for trail/ultra standards with 99% soft surface single-track dirt trail. An excellent race for first-time trail and ultramarathoners\, offering challenging terrain and panoramic views. Races run October 3-4\, 2026\, with the 100K and 50 Mile starting on Saturday and shorter distances on Sunday.
LOCATION:Bear Creek Lake Park\, Big Soda Lake Beach\, 15600 W. Morrison Road\, Lakewood\, CO
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:windsor-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260927T000000Z
DTSTART:20261004T070000Z
DTEND:20261004T110000Z
SUMMARY:Windsor Marathon
DESCRIPTION:Windsor Marathon events presented by Banner MD Anderson featuring multiple distances from 1 Mile Fit & Fun Run to full Marathon. Includes finisher lunch\, beverages\, finisher shirts and medals\, and an after party with food\, drinks\, music\, and kids zone. Proceeds benefit local nonprofits including Banner MD Anderson Cancer Center and Weld RE-4 Foundation.
LOCATION:The Island at Pelican Lakes\, Water Valley\, Windsor\, CO 80550
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:durango-marathon-2026@milehighrunners.com
DTSTAMP:20260927T000000Z
DTSTART:20261011T073000Z
DTEND:20261011T113000Z
SUMMARY:Durango Marathon
DESCRIPTION:Colorado's newest fall classic inaugural running event featuring a marathon\, half marathon\, and 5K. Scenic road race through Durango's mountain communities with start and finish at Santa Rita Park along the Animas River. Course showcases views of the San Juan Mountains and peak fall foliage. Elevation starts at approximately 6\,500 feet and reaches nearly 6\,900 feet at highest point. Race supports the Durango Education Foundation with a portion of proceeds funding scholarships for local high school students.
LOCATION:Santa Rita Park\, 111 South Camino Del Rio\, Durango\, CO 81301
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
